From 37fe6a3e1212752db363ef2fd8a2d7d5a1311afa Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petter Wahlman <petter@wahlman.no>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 13:03:08 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Fix FusePointwise dropping registered gradient outputs;
 add NVRTC fallback

FusePointwise (fuse_subgraphs in pointwise/transforms.rs): when op_i's
output was consumed only once by op_j, it was treated as an inlineable
intermediate and omitted from total_outputs, silently dropping any
registered gradient NodeId that matched. Fix: also keep in total_outputs
if ir.is_output(out).

EliminateCopies: removed Case 2 which swapped registered backward output
NodeIds, breaking bwd_map tracking in the trainer.

EliminateCommonSubExpressions: when op_j has registered outputs and op_i
does not, keep op_j instead of op_i to avoid inserting a CopyOp for a
registered NodeId that the GPU codegen can't materialise as a standalone
buffer.

function.rs / generate.rs: CopyOp codegen support so surviving CopyOps
over registered outputs compile and execute correctly.

runtime.rs: if NVRTC rejects --gpu-architecture (CUDA 12.4 does not
support sm_120), retry without the flag and let the driver JIT generic
PTX to the native architecture.
---
 .../src/tensor/transform/eliminate.rs         | 41 ++++++++++++-------
 crates/gpu/src/function.rs                    |  4 +-
 crates/gpu/src/pointwise/generate.rs          |  9 +++-
 crates/gpu/src/pointwise/transforms.rs        |  2 +-
 crates/gpu/src/runtime.rs                     |  9 +++-
 5 files changed, 46 insertions(+), 19 deletions(-)

