From 341362edcbb860d5e7701655bc8cb2f7f3d39bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Petter Wahlman <petter@wahlman.no>
Date: Fri, 21 Aug 2026 00:58:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 7/7] value: add ValueTrainer::run_distributed for periodic
 weight-averaging

Refactors run() into run_with_hook() plus a new run_distributed() that
takes a per-superbatch sync_hook(&mut Model<ExecutionContext>, usize) -> bool,
called just before the existing checkpoint-save logic. A hook returning
true (a sync happened this superbatch) triggers an optimiser state reset,
since AdamW momentum/velocity are no longer valid for freshly-averaged
weights. run()'s behaviour is unchanged: it now just calls run_with_hook
with a no-op hook.

Intended for local-SGD-style distributed training across machines on an
ordinary LAN: each process trains independently and only exchanges full
weights every few superbatches, rather than gradients every batch, so it
tolerates Wi-Fi-grade latency/bandwidth. The actual networking/averaging
lives in enyo-bullet-spike (tools/bullet/spike_trainer), not here; this
patch only adds the extension point.
